    "acceptanceCriteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "The result type exposes exactly six kinds and each lookup returns exactly one; the matched kind carries the handler, the path parameters, the actual method (the request method for a direct match, `GET` under automatic `HEAD` and for a WebSocket match; it does not decide the wave 3 `req.method()` value, D-398), the route kind and the automatic-`HEAD` flag, and the method-mismatch and automatic-OPTIONS kinds carry an `Allow` `MethodSet`. [D-390] [SDS 2026-10-19.naruserve.naruserve-v1-wave-2-3 SDS-AC-1] A field a kind does not carry reads as null (handler, method, route kind, allow) and params reads as an empty map.",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 940
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "An unrecognised method token yields unsupported method even when no pattern matches the path, and a recognised method on a path no pattern matches yields no match. [wave decision: lookup result order]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 941
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "On a matched path a route of the request method wins over automatic OPTIONS and automatic `HEAD`, which win over WebSocket-only, which wins over method mismatch. [wave decision: lookup result order]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 942
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-4",
        "text": "The lookup takes the raw, undecoded path as received in the request target, so a lookup of `GET /files/%252e` against `GET /files/:name` yields `name` = `%2e`; the path is checked with the path validator before any result is chosen, so a rejected path such as `/a%zz` fails with `IllegalArgumentException` for every method token, and \"whatever the path\" elsewhere in this scope means whatever accepted path. [D-051; loop W residual: validator does not decode] [SDS 2026-10-19.naruserve.naruserve-v1-wave-2-3 SDS-AC-2] The `IllegalArgumentException` names the path and is thrown before the method token is read.",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 943
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-5",
        "text": "The upgrade flag is ignored unless the method token is `GET`; registering a route after the freeze fails with `IllegalStateException`, a lookup before a successful freeze fails with `IllegalStateException`, and the routing configuration error is an exception type of its own (name decided under C-07), distinct from `IllegalStateException` and `IllegalArgumentException`. [wave decision: route kind; D-058]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 944
      }
    ],
